WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.700
You're probably familiar with

00:00:01.700 --> 00:00:03.800
the Meiji milk chocolate

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:05.300
on convenience store shelves today

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:06.500
, but you might not know

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:08.033
the story behind it:

00:00:08.033 --> 00:00:08.966
a poor boy

00:00:08.966 --> 00:00:11.066
's tale of rising to the top.

00:00:11.166 --> 00:00:13.166
How can a chocolate stand for

00:00:13.166 --> 00:00:14.133
a century? Why did Meiji, the birthplace of a Japanese brand

00:00:14.133 --> 00:00:16.266
, struggle in Taiwan

00:00:16.266 --> 00:00:17.666
during the

00:00:17.666 --> 00:00:18.666
fierce

00:00:18.666 --> 00:00:20.266
Japanese chocolate wars

00:00:20.333 --> 00:00:21.766
of the 1960s?

00:00:21.766 --> 00:00:24.000
How did it manage to carve out a path to survival

00:00:24.066 --> 00:00:25.333
? Hello, I'm Fat Cat.

00:00:25.366 --> 00:00:26.700
Today, let's talk about

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:28.133
the story of

00:00:28.133 --> 00:00:29.566
Meiji, the century-old

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:30.733
milk chocolate.

00:00:32.866 --> 00:00:34.800
In 1869, Soma Hanji was born into

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:36.133
a samurai family

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:37.333
in Aichi Prefecture.

00:00:37.366 --> 00:00:38.300
His family

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:39.800
had been retainers of the Inuyama Domain for

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:41.366
generations . Those familiar

00:00:41.366 --> 00:00:42.333
with Japanese history

00:00:42.333 --> 00:00:45.933
know that the year before Soma Hanji's birth, in 1868,

00:00:45.933 --> 00:00:47.400
the Meiji Restoration broke out

00:00:47.466 --> 00:00:49.700
, shattering the samurai class's secure livelihood.

00:00:49.766 --> 00:00:50.633
Hanji's father then

00:00:50.633 --> 00:00:52.100
tried his hand at business.

00:00:52.366 --> 00:00:54.966
There's a Japanese term called "samurai merchant law,"

00:00:55.166 --> 00:00:56.333
a derogatory

00:00:56.333 --> 00:00:58.200
term meaning that being an amateur, arrogant

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:00.766
, and bad at business inevitably leads to bankruptcy.

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:02.533
This perfectly describes his father and other

00:01:02.533 --> 00:01:04.266
samurai-born merchants.

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:05.666
The result was predictable:

00:01:05.766 --> 00:01:08.133
within a few years, they lost everything.

00:01:08.166 --> 00:01:10.333
Hungry and destitute

00:01:10.333 --> 00:01:11.733
in the slums

00:01:12.133 --> 00:01:13.700
, Hanji Soma's mother died

00:01:13.733 --> 00:01:15.066
when he was five,

00:01:15.133 --> 00:01:16.966
so his father sent him

00:01:16.966 --> 00:01:18.300
to live with his grandmother in

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:19.333
Nagoya. Hanji's

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:20.933
entire childhood

00:01:20.933 --> 00:01:22.266
was incredibly miserable

00:01:22.333 --> 00:01:23.633
, so from a young age he

00:01:23.633 --> 00:01:25.533
was single-mindedly focused on climbing the social

00:01:25.566 --> 00:01:26.733
ladder and getting ahead. His

00:01:26.866 --> 00:01:28.100
desire for success

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:29.366
was almost pathological

00:01:29.466 --> 00:01:31.066
; he was a very ambitious person.

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:32.233
In 1885,

00:01:32.233 --> 00:01:34.300
at the age of 17, Hanji decided to join the army.

00:01:34.366 --> 00:01:37.100
At that time, the Meiji government was obsessed with the idea of ​​"

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:38.000
enriching the country and strengthening

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:39.366
the army." The army offered many opportunities

00:01:39.366 --> 00:01:41.500
and was the only "elevator" for poor children to move up

00:01:41.566 --> 00:01:43.933
. Hideki Tojo's father, Hideyoshi Tojo, and

00:01:44.133 --> 00:01:45.400
Prime Minister Giichi Tanaka

00:01:45.466 --> 00:01:47.666
both started from the Army Training Corps,

00:01:47.666 --> 00:01:49.533
rising through the ranks from common soldier to

00:01:49.866 --> 00:01:52.300
high-ranking officer. Hanji Soma also wanted to join the Army Training Corps

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:53.866
, but regulations stipulated

00:01:53.866 --> 00:01:55.800
that applicants had to be at least 20 years old.

00:01:55.933 --> 00:01:57.333
Hanji, only 17,

00:01:57.366 --> 00:01:59.666
secretly altered his identification documents and

00:01:59.666 --> 00:02:02.100
entered by lying about his age. Once

00:02:02.166 --> 00:02:03.700
in the military, he endured rigorous training.

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:04.766
Undeterred by hardship, Hanji

00:02:04.766 --> 00:02:06.000
trained relentlessly every day.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:07.533
Later, in his autobiography, he said that

00:02:07.533 --> 00:02:09.000
compared to his time in the army,

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:10.933
the hardships of running a business were nothing.

00:02:11.166 --> 00:02:12.733
After serving as a common soldier for three years,

00:02:12.733 --> 00:02:15.500
in 1888 he applied to the officer cadet school.

00:02:15.533 --> 00:02:16.933
His superior 's recommendation review

00:02:16.933 --> 00:02:18.100
stated that he

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:19.466
was not qualified to be a general,

00:02:19.566 --> 00:02:21.400
effectively blocking his path.

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:22.133
Why?

00:02:22.133 --> 00:02:23.200
Later, in the army,

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:24.666
his friends joked that

00:02:24.666 --> 00:02:26.533
he probably trained too hard.

00:02:26.533 --> 00:02:27.166
In truth,

00:02:27.266 --> 00:02:29.766
people in the army also thought he was too pretentious,

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:31.000
but Hanji

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:31.800
wouldn't care

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:32.966
, much less give up.

00:02:32.966 --> 00:02:33.900
Since military service didn't work

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:34.700
, he turned to academics, studying

00:02:34.733 --> 00:02:36.900
with all his might. He

00:02:36.966 --> 00:02:38.133
was truly exceptional,

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:39.100
and soon

00:02:39.133 --> 00:02:41.866
entered the Applied Chemistry Department of Tokyo Technical School.

00:02:41.933 --> 00:02:43.066
Due to his outstanding grades,

00:02:43.066 --> 00:02:45.566
he graduated in 1896 and stayed on to teach,

00:02:45.566 --> 00:02:46.800
finally attracting the attention of

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:48.266
the school's principal,

00:02:48.266 --> 00:02:49.600
Teshima Seiichi.

00:02:49.766 --> 00:02:51.000
He climbed this tree. Teshima Seiichi was

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:53.700
a famous educator and Ministry of Education official

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:56.000
during the Meiji period,

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:58.700
with publicly funded overseas study opportunities.

00:02:58.733 --> 00:03:00.433
In 1899, Teshima Seiichi

00:03:00.433 --> 00:03:01.800
recommended him to go abroad for three years

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:02.766
to specialize in sugar production.

00:03:02.966 --> 00:03:04.133
It was also in this year that

00:03:04.133 --> 00:03:05.033
he received a letter from his hometown

00:03:05.033 --> 00:03:06.333
saying that his father was dying

00:03:06.333 --> 00:03:07.166
. Did he go back?

00:03:07.166 --> 00:03:08.600
No, he didn't even glance at

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:09.566
the door. Going abroad

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:12.533
was the most important thing . In fact, since the day he left home at the age of 17,

00:03:12.533 --> 00:03:14.300
he had never returned for a single day.

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:15.266
Even years later , when

00:03:15.266 --> 00:03:16.366
he was building a factory in Taiwan

00:03:16.366 --> 00:03:18.166
and his eldest son died of pneumonia,

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:20.900
his wife sent him a telegram urging him to come home, but he always said,

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:22.933
"I have important company business to attend to

00:03:22.933 --> 00:03:24.200
. Let the doctor handle it.

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:25.666
" You see,

00:03:25.666 --> 00:03:26.933
isn't this guy

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:28.366
extraordinary?

00:03:28.366 --> 00:03:30.666
Anyway, after that, he went from Java to Germany

00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:32.766
and then to the University of Michigan in the United States for

00:03:32.766 --> 00:03:35.366
further studies. In 1903, Soma Hanji returned to Japan,

00:03:35.366 --> 00:03:36.666
completely transformed.

00:03:36.666 --> 00:03:39.100
He became a professor at the Tokyo Higher Technical School.

00:03:39.133 --> 00:03:41.733
Students could always see him in a fashionable Western suit,

00:03:41.733 --> 00:03:43.366
leisurely riding a women's bicycle

00:03:43.366 --> 00:03:45.300
around the campus. After the First Sino

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:46.933
-Japanese War

00:03:46.933 --> 00:03:48.700
, Taiwan became a Japanese colony.

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:49.600
In 1899,

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:51.333
the Governor-General of Taiwan, Kodama Gentaro

00:03:51.333 --> 00:03:53.133
, and the Civil Administrator, Goto Shinpei,

00:03:53.133 --> 00:03:55.966
were eager to build a modern sugar factory in Taiwan.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:57.800
Goto Shinpei went to Tokyo

00:03:57.800 --> 00:03:59.800
and found... Inoue Kaoru and Shibusawa Eiichi

00:03:59.866 --> 00:04:02.533
even invited Mitsui's owner, Masuda Takaya, to

00:04:02.533 --> 00:04:03.333
a gathering .

00:04:03.333 --> 00:04:04.300
They said, "Old Masuda,

00:04:04.333 --> 00:04:05.966
Taiwan is a land of opportunity

00:04:05.966 --> 00:04:07.566
! Go there and set up a sugar factory.

00:04:07.566 --> 00:04:09.133
The Governor-General will fully support

00:04:09.333 --> 00:04:10.966
you, brother. You 'll have a monopoly on

00:04:10.966 --> 00:04:12.200
Mitsui products,

00:04:12.366 --> 00:04:13.266
guaranteed profits.

00:04:13.333 --> 00:04:14.366
We brothers

00:04:14.366 --> 00:04:15.866
can also make a little money along the way."

00:04:16.133 --> 00:04:18.300
Thus, in December 1900,

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:19.933
the Taiwan Sugar Corporation

00:04:19.933 --> 00:04:21.200
was officially established.

00:04:21.266 --> 00:04:24.466
The following year, Taiwan's first modern mechanized sugar factory

00:04:24.466 --> 00:04:26.066
broke ground in Kaohsiung,

00:04:26.066 --> 00:04:28.966
marking the beginning of Taiwan's modern sugar industry.

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:31.166
In 1904, the Governor-General's office found

00:04:31.166 --> 00:04:32.600
Soma Hanji, who had just returned from Japan,

00:04:32.700 --> 00:04:34.400
and hired him to provide technical guidance.

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:35.300
Upon arriving in Taiwan,

00:04:35.366 --> 00:04:36.666
Hanji immediately understood that

00:04:36.733 --> 00:04:37.800
the sugar business

00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:39.700
was a lucrative colonial venture.

00:04:39.966 --> 00:04:41.600
Why? Because the following year,

00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:43.333
the Taiwan Governor-General's office issued

00:04:43.333 --> 00:04:45.000
regulations to prohibit sugar production

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:47.466
, stipulating that sugarcane farmers could only sell their sugarcane to

00:04:47.466 --> 00:04:49.366
sugar companies within designated areas.

00:04:49.566 --> 00:04:51.800
The prices were determined by the companies themselves

00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:53.366
and were often arbitrarily lowered.

00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:55.566
There's a Taiwanese proverb that goes, "

00:04:55.566 --> 00:04:57.933
The first fool plants sugarcane, the second is the scale. "

00:04:58.200 --> 00:04:58.800
So you see,

00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:01.666
this is a business monopolized by colonial policies.

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:03.600
Soma Hanji wanted to get involved

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:05.566
, but he was just a technician

00:05:05.566 --> 00:05:06.500
and didn't have the resources.

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:08.466
A key element here

00:05:08.466 --> 00:05:09.466
is shipping.

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:11.500
Why could Mitsui do this business?

00:05:11.666 --> 00:05:14.366
Why did the Governor-General's Office initially approach Mitsui?

00:05:14.466 --> 00:05:16.766
Because they had shipping resources.

00:05:16.866 --> 00:05:18.533
If you open a sugar factory in Taiwan

00:05:18.533 --> 00:05:20.900
and then have Mitsui handle your shipping,

00:05:20.900 --> 00:05:21.966
it's better not to do it

00:05:22.266 --> 00:05:24.700
at all. So, as soon as Hanji returned to Japan, he approached

00:05:24.700 --> 00:05:27.266
Ogawa Takichi, a director of Nippon Yusen

00:05:27.366 --> 00:05:29.366
. Ogawa was backed by the Mitsubishi zaibatsu.

00:05:29.500 --> 00:05:30.666
The two were from the same hometown

00:05:30.866 --> 00:05:33.600
. Hanji went to Ogawa every day to curry favor,

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:34.466
boasting, "

00:05:34.466 --> 00:05:35.366
Brother Ogawa,

00:05:35.366 --> 00:05:36.200
I have the technology

00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:38.100
and connections with the Governor-General's Office.

00:05:38.133 --> 00:05:39.700
Why should Mitsui monopolize

00:05:39.700 --> 00:05:41.400
the Taiwanese sugar business?

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:42.566
You and your boss

00:05:42.566 --> 00:05:43.600
should talk to them.

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:45.900
How about we set up a refined sugar factory

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:46.533
?"

00:05:46.566 --> 00:05:48.733
But Ogawa completely looked down on him.

00:05:48.766 --> 00:05:50.466
His connections were worthless.

00:05:50.466 --> 00:05:52.533
Several times when he came to Ogawa's door, he directly started cursing.

00:05:52.566 --> 00:05:53.800
"I didn't sleep well last night

00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:55.166
and don't want to see anyone~ Get lost~"

00:05:55.533 --> 00:05:56.966
But Hanji Soma

00:05:56.966 --> 00:05:58.533
was a notoriously hot-tempered man,

00:05:58.533 --> 00:06:01.366
later known as "Typhoon Soma" in the factory for his

00:06:01.466 --> 00:06:03.133
extremely strict management style.

00:06:03.133 --> 00:06:04.500
However, in front of Ogawa,

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:05.833
he trampled all his pride

00:06:05.833 --> 00:06:07.166
underfoot,

00:06:07.333 --> 00:06:08.000
never fighting back

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:08.866
or arguing.

00:06:08.866 --> 00:06:09.900
When Ogawa told him to get lost

00:06:09.900 --> 00:06:11.266
, he would still come back the next day.

00:06:11.266 --> 00:06:13.966
In the end, he managed to move Ogawa.

00:06:13.966 --> 00:06:16.366
In his later years, Hanji Soma wrote in his autobiography,

00:06:16.366 --> 00:06:18.066
"My two benefactors in life

00:06:18.066 --> 00:06:19.733
are Teshima Seiichi, who took me abroad,

00:06:19.733 --> 00:06:22.266
and Ogawa Takichi, who led me into the business world."

00:06:22.566 --> 00:06:23.666
After moving Ogawa,

00:06:23.666 --> 00:06:24.666
things went smoothly.

00:06:24.666 --> 00:06:26.666
Ogawa used his connections with the Mitsubishi Group

00:06:26.666 --> 00:06:29.466
to bring in Shibusawa Eiichi and Morimura Ichizaemon, the

00:06:29.466 --> 00:06:32.300
Morimura zaibatsu we've mentioned before. The TOTO tycoon

00:06:32.333 --> 00:06:34.966
raised 5 million yen in principal in one fell swoop.

00:06:35.066 --> 00:06:37.500
Ogawa himself took charge in Tokyo as president, and only then...

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:39.166
Unwilling to go to Taiwan to eat dirt

00:06:39.466 --> 00:06:42.066
, Soma Hanji charged ahead and went to Taiwan.

00:06:42.066 --> 00:06:43.700
In December 1906,

00:06:43.766 --> 00:06:46.400
Meiji Sugar officially opened in Tainan.

00:06:46.466 --> 00:06:49.500
This is the origin of today's Meiji.

00:06:50.200 --> 00:06:51.700
Entering the 1910s,

00:06:51.700 --> 00:06:54.400
Taiwanese sugar factories ushered in a period of crazy expansion.

00:06:54.400 --> 00:06:56.133
The four major giants were all in place

00:06:56.166 --> 00:06:57.866
, each with its own path,

00:06:57.866 --> 00:06:59.400
frantically grabbing land and sugarcane.

00:06:59.566 --> 00:07:02.066
Unfortunately, those years coincided with World War I, when

00:07:02.066 --> 00:07:03.300
European sugar supplies were cut off, and

00:07:03.333 --> 00:07:06.266
Taiwan's sugar production soared to its historical peak.

00:07:06.466 --> 00:07:07.900
But Hanji knew that

00:07:07.933 --> 00:07:09.366
sugar was a bulk raw material,

00:07:09.366 --> 00:07:10.733
and the price mainly depended on market

00:07:10.766 --> 00:07:12.133
fluctuations

00:07:12.133 --> 00:07:13.733
. It was good now

00:07:13.733 --> 00:07:15.900
, but the boom would eventually pass.

00:07:16.066 --> 00:07:18.400
In 1915, the first president, Ogawa,

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:20.800
officially handed over the position to Soma Hanji.

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:22.000
After nearly 10 years,

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:23.866
this guy finally made it.

00:07:23.866 --> 00:07:25.966
In 1916, he had ambition Bo Bo

00:07:25.966 --> 00:07:27.533
presented the board with a

00:07:27.533 --> 00:07:29.100
report on the confectionery business.

00:07:29.333 --> 00:07:30.333
The central idea was

00:07:30.333 --> 00:07:31.633
that instead of selling all the sugar

00:07:31.633 --> 00:07:33.900
to local grocery stores and factories

00:07:33.900 --> 00:07:35.266
and relying on their whims

00:07:35.300 --> 00:07:37.333
, it would be better to move downstream and

00:07:37.400 --> 00:07:38.600
open a candy factory.

00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:40.500
Firstly, this would reduce

00:07:40.500 --> 00:07:42.000
the impact of market price fluctuations on the company's profits.

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:43.600
Secondly, Japan

00:07:43.600 --> 00:07:46.166
was currently experiencing a wave of Westernization;

00:07:46.300 --> 00:07:49.600
Western milk chocolate and candies were all fashionable.

00:07:49.600 --> 00:07:50.733
Our sugar

00:07:50.733 --> 00:07:51.900
only sold for a few dollars

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:54.166
a pound , but once mixed with cocoa and milk,

00:07:54.166 --> 00:07:56.166
its value increased dozens of times.

00:07:56.300 --> 00:07:57.366
Look at Morinaga;

00:07:57.366 --> 00:07:58.900
they made more money than us

00:07:59.100 --> 00:08:01.166
with just one box of Morinaga milk candy,

00:08:01.166 --> 00:08:02.566
even though they sourced it from us !

00:08:02.666 --> 00:08:03.766
Morinaga Taichiro,

00:08:03.800 --> 00:08:06.333
who couldn't even make a living selling broken pottery,

00:08:06.333 --> 00:08:07.133
what makes him so special?

00:08:07.133 --> 00:08:08.900
Meiji should do

00:08:08.900 --> 00:08:10.566
a vertically integrated business, from production to sales.

00:08:10.666 --> 00:08:13.000
Not a single penny of profit would be leaked to outsiders

00:08:13.000 --> 00:08:15.866
—this was the grand Meiji strategy he proposed.

00:08:16.100 --> 00:08:16.866
Upon hearing this, the board

00:08:16.866 --> 00:08:18.600
applauded, saying, "Excellent

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:20.666
! Soma is indeed far-sighted!

00:08:20.666 --> 00:08:21.500
Let's do it!"

00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:24.766
In 1916, Meiji Sugar established a new company

00:08:24.766 --> 00:08:26.966
called Tokyo Seika Co., Ltd.

00:08:26.966 --> 00:08:29.666
, the predecessor of Meiji Seika.

00:08:31.600 --> 00:08:34.666
If you were in Tokyo in the 1920s

00:08:34.666 --> 00:08:35.933
and randomly asked a passerby

00:08:35.933 --> 00:08:37.500
which Japanese chocolate brand was the best

00:08:37.566 --> 00:08:38.833
, eight out of ten

00:08:38.833 --> 00:08:40.500
would tell you the name Morinaga.

00:08:40.600 --> 00:08:43.566
Why? Because in 1918, Morinaga produced

00:08:43.566 --> 00:08:45.500
Japan's first domestically made chocolate,

00:08:45.566 --> 00:08:46.666
gaining an absolute first-mover advantage

00:08:46.666 --> 00:08:48.500
in the chocolate market

00:08:48.566 --> 00:08:49.366
and leading

00:08:49.600 --> 00:08:50.900
the pack. Looking at Soma Hanji

00:08:51.066 --> 00:08:52.000
, he wasn't discouraged.

00:08:52.266 --> 00:08:54.933
Meiji's strategy was to first cultivate the confectionery market and

00:08:54.933 --> 00:08:56.200
temporarily avoid chocolate,

00:08:56.300 --> 00:08:57.100
developing cautiously.

00:08:57.133 --> 00:08:59.266
After all... Upstream manufacturers,

00:08:59.266 --> 00:09:00.400
facing the consumer market,

00:09:00.400 --> 00:09:02.200
were not as cunning as Morinaga.

00:09:02.333 --> 00:09:04.533
So, while refining their production capacity and distribution channels, they

00:09:04.533 --> 00:09:05.900
waited for the right opportunity.

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:07.500
Tokyo Confectionery's annual revenue was less than

00:09:07.500 --> 00:09:09.300
60,000 yen when it was first established

00:09:09.333 --> 00:09:11.333
. In just a few years, by 1924,

00:09:11.333 --> 00:09:13.966
its revenue had soared to 6 million yen.

00:09:14.266 --> 00:09:16.466
In 1925, Meiji began to make a big move.

00:09:16.533 --> 00:09:17.600
The Kawasaki factory was completed

00:09:17.600 --> 00:09:18.800
, marking Meiji's first

00:09:18.800 --> 00:09:20.800
large-scale modern confectionery factory.

00:09:20.866 --> 00:09:21.700
With the factory secured, Meiji turned

00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:23.933
its attention to the raw material problem.

00:09:23.933 --> 00:09:25.300
Japan did not produce cocoa beans

00:09:25.366 --> 00:09:26.866
and relied entirely on imports through intermediaries.

00:09:26.900 --> 00:09:29.100
Soma Hanji bypassed all intermediaries

00:09:29.133 --> 00:09:30.933
and directly connected with overseas production areas

00:09:31.100 --> 00:09:33.200
, securing a high-quality source of goods.

00:09:33.200 --> 00:09:34.866
Then, they invested heavily in upgrading equipment,

00:09:34.866 --> 00:09:36.800
specifically importing

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:39.066
a complete set of the most advanced chocolate machines

00:09:39.066 --> 00:09:41.066
from Germany. They also poached the German master craftsman

00:09:41.066 --> 00:09:42.466
Casper to work in the factory at a high salary.

00:09:42.733 --> 00:09:45.133
At that time, Japan... A common problem with domestically produced chocolate

00:09:45.200 --> 00:09:46.333
is that chocolate is oily

00:09:46.333 --> 00:09:47.666
while milk is watery.

00:09:47.666 --> 00:09:48.866
If the mixing

00:09:48.866 --> 00:09:51.600
process isn't done properly, it will have a milky, fishy taste.

00:09:51.800 --> 00:09:53.333
Caspar introduced a unique

00:09:53.333 --> 00:09:55.200
German-style whole milk powder blending process,

00:09:55.200 --> 00:09:57.900
allowing Meiji to create

00:09:57.900 --> 00:09:59.266
pure milk chocolate

00:09:59.333 --> 00:10:01.633
without adding a single drop of water . The most difficult step in this process

00:10:01.633 --> 00:10:02.800
is tempering the chocolate,

00:10:03.133 --> 00:10:04.600
ensuring the cocoa butter crystals

00:10:04.666 --> 00:10:06.300
are neatly arranged.

00:10:06.400 --> 00:10:07.333
When the crystals are properly aligned, the chocolate will

00:10:07.400 --> 00:10:09.033
break with

00:10:09.033 --> 00:10:10.500
a crisp "pop" sound

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:12.500
and melt instantly in your mouth,

00:10:12.500 --> 00:10:13.500
resulting in a silky smooth texture.

00:10:13.533 --> 00:10:14.933
If the tempering isn't done correctly,

00:10:14.933 --> 00:10:15.733
the crystals will be disordered,

00:10:15.800 --> 00:10:17.000
the chocolate surface will turn white,

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:18.266
and the taste will be terrible.

00:10:18.566 --> 00:10:20.400
Meiji's technicians refined the process repeatedly,

00:10:20.466 --> 00:10:21.766
conducting countless experiments.

00:10:21.800 --> 00:10:24.400
Finally, on September 13, 1926,

00:10:24.566 --> 00:10:26.766
Meiji milk chocolate was officially born

00:10:26.900 --> 00:10:29.200
. Then, Meiji began to focus its efforts...

00:10:29.500 --> 00:10:31.133
In 1929, Meiji

00:10:31.133 --> 00:10:33.200
opened its first directly operated brand store in Taiwan

00:10:33.200 --> 00:10:35.166
. Its innovative marketing strategies, including prize draws and

00:10:35.166 --> 00:10:36.700
free samples,

00:10:36.800 --> 00:10:38.600
quickly boosted market awareness

00:10:38.600 --> 00:10:40.266
and brought it closer to consumers.

00:10:40.266 --> 00:10:41.533
By the end of 1931,

00:10:41.600 --> 00:10:44.100
Meiji had firmly established itself in the chocolate market,

00:10:44.100 --> 00:10:46.766
becoming Morinaga's most formidable competitor.

00:10:47.300 --> 00:10:49.400
In 1932, with the establishment of the puppet state of Manchukuo,

00:10:49.400 --> 00:10:51.400
Meiji, which had started with sugar trading

00:10:51.400 --> 00:10:52.533
in the Taiwanese colony,

00:10:52.533 --> 00:10:54.766
naturally wouldn't let go of this new lucrative market

00:10:54.766 --> 00:10:56.200
and expanded its business into Northeast

00:10:56.366 --> 00:10:59.466
China . In 1939, the Manchurian Meiji Confectionery Co., Ltd. was established.

00:10:59.466 --> 00:11:01.966
In 1942, it

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:04.200
merged with Manchurian Dairy, unifying the entire Manchurian Meiji industry.

00:11:04.200 --> 00:11:06.166
On the black soil of Northeast China,

00:11:06.266 --> 00:11:07.766
Meiji not only sold candy

00:11:07.766 --> 00:11:09.900
but also raised cows, milked them, and produced dairy products,

00:11:09.900 --> 00:11:11.500
gradually forming

00:11:11.500 --> 00:11:13.100
a complete sugar and dairy food empire

00:11:13.333 --> 00:11:14.566
. As the war intensified,

00:11:14.600 --> 00:11:17.500
all food companies were brought under controlled economic

00:11:17.600 --> 00:11:19.933
management. Meiji began to massively shift production to military rations and

00:11:19.966 --> 00:11:21.166
nutritional field biscuits.

00:11:21.200 --> 00:11:22.766
From 1944 to 1945,

00:11:22.766 --> 00:11:24.900
American bombers flew over the Japanese mainland,

00:11:24.900 --> 00:11:25.966
and the Tokyo air raids

00:11:26.133 --> 00:11:27.966
destroyed factories across the country,

00:11:27.966 --> 00:11:29.166
essentially paralyzing production capacity.

00:11:29.400 --> 00:11:31.400
On January 7, 1946,

00:11:31.533 --> 00:11:33.933
Meiji's founder, Hanji Soma, passed away

00:11:34.066 --> 00:11:35.400
at the age of 78.

00:11:35.500 --> 00:11:39.200
In the same year, the Nationalist government merged the four major Japanese sugar companies in Taiwan

00:11:39.200 --> 00:11:41.166
into the Taiwan Sugar Corporation.

00:11:41.533 --> 00:11:42.966
The sugar industry had originated in Taiwan, and

00:11:43.066 --> 00:11:44.700
the dairy industry had expanded from Northeast

00:11:44.700 --> 00:11:47.300
China. With these two colonial foundations severed,

00:11:47.333 --> 00:11:48.866
Meiji retreated to the mainland.

00:11:48.933 --> 00:11:51.166
By this time, its scale was much smaller than before. In

00:11:52.766 --> 00:11:54.766
1951, with the post-war reconstruction underway,

00:11:54.766 --> 00:11:57.300
Meiji, which had been dormant for a long time, decided

00:11:57.300 --> 00:11:58.666
to fight a revival battle on the ruins.

00:11:58.666 --> 00:11:59.400
The first step

00:11:59.400 --> 00:12:01.900
was to bring back its most classic and ace product

00:12:01.900 --> 00:12:04.400
from before the war. Meiji milk chocolate returned to the shelves.

00:12:04.466 --> 00:12:05.100
This chocolate, created in 1926

00:12:05.100 --> 00:12:07.100
during the war,

00:12:07.100 --> 00:12:08.666
had disappeared for many years.

00:12:08.866 --> 00:12:10.533
Meiji wanted to use it to tell the market

00:12:10.533 --> 00:12:11.533
they were still alive

00:12:11.600 --> 00:12:13.800
and to rekindle consumer memories.

00:12:13.866 --> 00:12:15.333
In the mid-1950s,

00:12:15.366 --> 00:12:17.166
the Japanese economy began to recover.

00:12:17.200 --> 00:12:19.066
The special orders brought by the Korean War

00:12:19.066 --> 00:12:21.333
revitalized the manufacturing industry, and

00:12:21.466 --> 00:12:23.333
the long-dormant consumer market

00:12:23.333 --> 00:12:24.366
also saw a revival. Meiji

00:12:24.666 --> 00:12:26.666
seized the opportunity and launched its second product:

00:12:26.700 --> 00:12:29.666
the deluxe milk chocolate in 1957.

00:12:29.733 --> 00:12:32.133
Its core selling point was simply "thicker." Previously

00:12:32.466 --> 00:12:34.500
, slab chocolates were generally thin,

00:12:34.500 --> 00:12:36.066
mainly due to raw material shortages.

00:12:36.166 --> 00:12:37.533
This thick slab chocolate

00:12:37.533 --> 00:12:40.100
gave consumers a more substantial feel

00:12:40.100 --> 00:12:42.000
and quickly became a bestseller.

00:12:42.133 --> 00:12:45.166
Following this, Meiji turned its attention to the children's market and

00:12:45.166 --> 00:12:46.300
launched its third product:

00:12:46.566 --> 00:12:48.800
the colorful ball chocolate in 1961.

00:12:48.900 --> 00:12:51.366
Seven colors of sugar coating wrapped around the chocolate

00:12:51.466 --> 00:12:54.066
tubes in innovative packaging, making them a striking addition

00:12:54.066 --> 00:12:55.333
to the shelves.

00:12:55.333 --> 00:12:56.566
But Meiji's ambitions

00:12:56.566 --> 00:12:58.900
went far beyond product innovation.

00:12:59.133 --> 00:13:00.700
Two years later, in 1963,

00:13:00.700 --> 00:13:02.733
Astro Boy swept across Japan.

00:13:02.733 --> 00:13:05.333
As the core sponsor of this groundbreaking animation,

00:13:05.466 --> 00:13:07.133
Meiji executed a

00:13:07.133 --> 00:13:09.766
classic campaign that can be considered the progenitor of modern IP marketing.

00:13:09.966 --> 00:13:11.566
They directly printed Astro Boy's image

00:13:11.566 --> 00:13:13.933
on the packaging of their colorful chocolate balls and

00:13:13.933 --> 00:13:15.666
included different Astro Boy collectible stickers

00:13:15.666 --> 00:13:18.066
inside each product

00:13:18.133 --> 00:13:20.666
. With fun snacks and popular anime merchandise,

00:13:20.766 --> 00:13:22.500
the colorful chocolate balls quickly became

00:13:22.500 --> 00:13:24.766
a phenomenal children's snack in the Showa era.

00:13:24.900 --> 00:13:27.100
In 1963 alone,

00:13:27.133 --> 00:13:29.933
sales soared to 5.8 billion yen.

00:13:30.200 --> 00:13:33.166
Meiji captured a whopping 38% market share

00:13:33.166 --> 00:13:35.300
in the Japanese chocolate market

00:13:35.466 --> 00:13:36.933
, firmly establishing itself as the industry leader.

00:13:37.466 --> 00:13:38.800
At this very moment,

00:13:38.866 --> 00:13:41.066
wolves in the shadows were raising their heads.

00:13:41.100 --> 00:13:42.633
The first to bare their fangs

00:13:42.633 --> 00:13:44.766
was Meiji's century-old rival, Morinaga.

00:13:44.866 --> 00:13:48.500
In the 1960s, the Japanese chocolate market was in full swing. In

00:13:48.733 --> 00:13:49.666
1964,

00:13:49.733 --> 00:13:52.333
Morinaga launched the highly disruptive Hi CROWN.

00:13:52.466 --> 00:13:55.300
In an era when ordinary chocolates only sold for 50 yen,

00:13:55.333 --> 00:13:57.766
Hi CROWN... CROWN, priced at 70 yen,

00:13:58.000 --> 00:14:00.166
focused on high-end ingredients and a sophisticated taste

00:14:00.266 --> 00:14:02.933
, using hard-shell packaging similar to luxury cigarette boxes.

00:14:03.000 --> 00:14:05.366
This strikingly modern visual impact

00:14:05.366 --> 00:14:08.166
quickly won over the urban elites who had grown up after the war.

00:14:08.466 --> 00:14:09.300
Morinaga's move

00:14:09.300 --> 00:14:11.266
directly plunging the market into

00:14:11.266 --> 00:14:13.000
a high-end category that Meiji had never ventured into

00:14:13.000 --> 00:14:15.500
. Before Meiji could even recover,

00:14:15.566 --> 00:14:17.200
in 1964,

00:14:17.200 --> 00:14:18.733
the ambitious Shin Kyuk-hiro

00:14:18.933 --> 00:14:20.666
led Lotte into the fray,

00:14:20.666 --> 00:14:22.466
launching Ghana milk chocolate.

00:14:22.566 --> 00:14:23.366
On its release day,

00:14:23.366 --> 00:14:25.400
groups of female university students carrying bright red

00:14:25.400 --> 00:14:27.066
handbags

00:14:27.066 --> 00:14:28.733
paraded through the streets of Tokyo for an entire week

00:14:28.733 --> 00:14:30.633
—a masterclass in street marketing.

00:14:30.633 --> 00:14:33.366
Lotte's rise to prominence as the focus of the entire city

00:14:33.566 --> 00:14:36.666
was clearly a head-on confrontation

00:14:36.666 --> 00:14:39.366
with Meiji's established chocolate base.

00:14:39.400 --> 00:14:41.266
The offensive was far from over.

00:14:41.333 --> 00:14:43.600
In 1966, Glico took a different approach

00:14:43.600 --> 00:14:44.700
, launching Pocky,

00:14:44.700 --> 00:14:47.200
touted as the world's first stick-shaped chocolate snack.

00:14:47.500 --> 00:14:48.466
Unlike Lotte,

00:14:48.500 --> 00:14:49.533
Glico

00:14:49.533 --> 00:14:51.266
employed a sophisticated

00:14:51.266 --> 00:14:53.000
flanking strategy.

00:14:53.000 --> 00:14:55.566
Instead of directly competing in the traditional chocolate market, they

00:14:55.566 --> 00:14:58.100
pioneered a completely new consumption scenario: a

00:14:58.266 --> 00:15:00.366
lightweight snack that could be enjoyed on the go

00:15:00.466 --> 00:15:03.100
without getting chocolate on your fingers . Morinaga's high-altitude

00:15:03.366 --> 00:15:04.600
attack on Lotte's frontal assault

00:15:04.733 --> 00:15:06.066
and Glico's flanking maneuver

00:15:06.066 --> 00:15:07.600
left many sitting on

00:15:07.733 --> 00:15:09.933
the edge of their seats stunned. Meiji, now at the top,

00:15:09.933 --> 00:15:10.933
was besieged on all sides,

00:15:11.066 --> 00:15:11.966
facing

00:15:12.000 --> 00:15:12.933
a pincer attack

00:15:12.966 --> 00:15:14.900
aimed

00:15:15.133 --> 00:15:17.066
at its core. Meiji was thrown into disarray.

00:15:17.066 --> 00:15:17.933
In 1969,

00:15:17.933 --> 00:15:20.066
hastily responding

00:15:20.133 --> 00:15:21.100
to the challenge,

00:15:21.200 --> 00:15:22.100
Meiji launched

00:15:22.200 --> 00:15:24.133
a cone-shaped chocolate called Apollo,

00:15:24.166 --> 00:15:25.733
which sold poorly

00:15:25.733 --> 00:15:27.966
and received little response. This highly anticipated product

00:15:28.200 --> 00:15:29.633
not only failed to turn the tide

00:15:29.633 --> 00:15:31.600
but also became a hot potato within the company. Company

00:15:31.600 --> 00:15:32.333
executives

00:15:32.333 --> 00:15:34.466
held daily meetings debating whether to

00:15:34.466 --> 00:15:35.666
completely discontinue

00:15:35.766 --> 00:15:37.500
this money-losing product. Caught

00:15:37.733 --> 00:15:38.766
between

00:15:38.933 --> 00:15:40.166
tactical failure and internal pessimism,

00:15:40.166 --> 00:15:41.600
Meiji was pushed to the brink of collapse.

00:15:41.600 --> 00:15:43.733
At this critical moment, Meiji's R&amp;D team gambled their last hope,

00:15:43.733 --> 00:15:46.300
inserting... A stick-shaped biscuit appeared

00:15:46.300 --> 00:15:47.100
—what is this?

00:15:47.100 --> 00:15:48.566
Everyone exclaimed, "Mushroom!"

00:15:48.900 --> 00:15:49.866
In 1975,

00:15:49.866 --> 00:15:51.400
the famous Mushroom Mountain

00:15:51.400 --> 00:15:52.200
biscuit burst

00:15:52.266 --> 00:15:53.733
onto the scene and became an instant hit.

00:15:53.733 --> 00:15:55.466
Four years later, in 1979,

00:15:55.466 --> 00:15:56.766
Meiji

00:15:56.766 --> 00:15:59.800
followed up with Bamboo Shoot Village to compete with Mushroom Mountain.

00:15:59.800 --> 00:16:00.766
To outsiders, it seemed like a case

00:16:00.766 --> 00:16:02.466
of their own products fighting each other—

00:16:02.466 --> 00:16:03.966
wasn't that crazy?

00:16:03.966 --> 00:16:04.866
But in reality,

00:16:04.866 --> 00:16:07.700
this was Meiji's deeper business strategy.

00:16:07.933 --> 00:16:09.600
As Mushroom Mountain gained a foothold,

00:16:09.700 --> 00:16:11.233
Meiji keenly sensed that

00:16:11.233 --> 00:16:14.100
consumers' tastes were undergoing subtle changes.

00:16:14.100 --> 00:16:15.300
More dramatically, the question became:

00:16:15.300 --> 00:16:17.466
would you choose Mushroom Mountain or Bamboo Shoot Village?

00:16:17.466 --> 00:16:19.666
This was originally a question about taste, but

00:16:19.666 --> 00:16:21.800
in Japanese society, it gradually evolved into...

00:16:21.800 --> 00:16:23.600
A label of identity:

00:16:23.800 --> 00:16:26.766
This grassroots debate, which began around 1980,

00:16:26.766 --> 00:16:29.200
was jokingly referred to as the "Mushroom Wars."

00:16:29.300 --> 00:16:31.533
In 2001, Meiji

00:16:31.600 --> 00:16:32.933
officially launched

00:16:33.166 --> 00:16:35.100
a general election for mushrooms and bamboo shoots

00:16:35.100 --> 00:16:36.966
, igniting this grassroots spark

00:16:36.966 --> 00:16:39.000
. Buying chocolate became voting,

00:16:39.100 --> 00:16:40.733
and consumers transformed from ordinary customers

00:16:40.766 --> 00:16:42.733
into loyal party members. Today,

00:16:42.733 --> 00:16:44.233
the combined annual sales

00:16:44.233 --> 00:16:45.500
of these two products

00:16:45.500 --> 00:16:48.066
have reached approximately 23 billion yen.

00:16:48.333 --> 00:16:51.000
Meiji not only carved out a path for itself

00:16:51.000 --> 00:16:52.366
among Morinaga, Rakuten, and Glico,

00:16:52.366 --> 00:16:53.466
but also made this counterattack

00:16:53.466 --> 00:16:55.466
one of the most successful business cases

00:16:55.466 --> 00:16:56.966
in the history of modern Japanese marketing.

00:16:57.166 --> 00:16:58.800
However, the chocolate war

00:16:58.800 --> 00:17:01.500
was only half of Meiji's business empire.

00:17:01.500 --> 00:17:03.200
In the long years after the war,

00:17:03.266 --> 00:17:05.333
Meiji was actually two companies:

00:17:05.333 --> 00:17:08.166
Meiji Confectionery, which fought the chocolate war, and Meiji Dairy,

00:17:08.166 --> 00:17:10.100
which focused on milk

00:17:10.100 --> 00:17:12.000
and dairy products.

00:17:12.100 --> 00:17:14.066
Let's talk about this side.

00:17:14.300 --> 00:17:15.966
In 1946, Meiji Dairy

00:17:15.966 --> 00:17:17.666
quickly seized the opportunities of the times.

00:17:17.666 --> 00:17:18.766
They utilized the beauty... Using

00:17:18.766 --> 00:17:20.733
skim milk powder to make flavored milk, Meiji

00:17:20.733 --> 00:17:22.500
entered schools and households across Japan

00:17:22.566 --> 00:17:24.933
thanks to the country's economic recovery .

00:17:25.000 --> 00:17:26.300
An entire generation of Japanese children

00:17:26.300 --> 00:17:27.366
grew up drinking

00:17:27.366 --> 00:17:29.566
milk bearing the Meiji name.

00:17:29.700 --> 00:17:31.966
From dairy beverages to Bulgarian yogurt

00:17:31.966 --> 00:17:33.766
and then to the wildly popular ice cream,

00:17:33.933 --> 00:17:35.666
Meiji Dairy steadily built its business.

00:17:35.666 --> 00:17:37.300
Compared to the

00:17:37.300 --> 00:17:39.366
fiercely competitive chocolate market, which relied on high-profile marketing, its

00:17:39.400 --> 00:17:40.866
dairy business, though low-key

00:17:40.866 --> 00:17:42.733
, enjoyed extremely high consumption frequency.

00:17:42.933 --> 00:17:44.800
A bottle of milk was a daily

00:17:44.800 --> 00:17:46.000
necessity for many

00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:47.933
, providing Meiji with a more stable

00:17:47.933 --> 00:17:50.700
cash flow and stronger brand loyalty.

00:17:50.766 --> 00:17:52.333
For more than half a century after the war,

00:17:52.400 --> 00:17:53.800
chocolate and dairy products

00:17:53.800 --> 00:17:55.466
became Meiji's twin engines

00:17:55.466 --> 00:17:56.366
, propelling

00:17:56.366 --> 00:17:57.266
it forward

00:17:57.266 --> 00:17:59.500
and transforming it into a

00:17:59.500 --> 00:18:02.366
comprehensive food empire deeply rooted in the daily lives of the Japanese people.

00:18:02.933 --> 00:18:04.533
In the 1980s,

00:18:04.533 --> 00:18:06.766
having solidified its foundation in Japan,

00:18:06.766 --> 00:18:08.333
Meiji began to set its sights on

00:18:08.333 --> 00:18:09.900
broader overseas markets.

00:18:09.900 --> 00:18:11.333
Their first destination was...

00:18:11.333 --> 00:18:12.166
Meiji's

00:18:12.266 --> 00:18:13.333
return to the Taiwanese market still

00:18:13.333 --> 00:18:16.200
involved a strategic overseas expansion through licensing and agency agreements.

00:18:16.400 --> 00:18:17.100
In 1986,

00:18:17.100 --> 00:18:19.600
Meiji reached a technical cooperation agreement with Tailon Industrial,

00:18:19.733 --> 00:18:21.700
authorizing Tailon's Taoyuan production line

00:18:21.700 --> 00:18:24.333
to locally produce Meiji and Bagel ice creams.

00:18:24.400 --> 00:18:25.733
Since the 1980s,

00:18:25.733 --> 00:18:27.066
classic milk chocolate

00:18:27.066 --> 00:18:28.066
mushroom-shaped cookies and

00:18:28.066 --> 00:18:29.100
Apollo chocolate

00:18:29.100 --> 00:18:31.566
have never been out of stock on Taiwanese shelves.

00:18:31.766 --> 00:18:32.733
The name Meiji

00:18:32.733 --> 00:18:34.133
is deeply etched in

00:18:34.133 --> 00:18:36.000
the childhood memories of many Taiwanese.

00:18:36.200 --> 00:18:37.600
On the mainland,

00:18:37.600 --> 00:18:39.666
Meiji has also woven a vast network.

00:18:39.700 --> 00:18:41.566
In 1994, Meiji

00:18:41.566 --> 00:18:43.866
established its first joint venture

00:18:44.100 --> 00:18:44.933
in Guangzhou. This marked the beginning

00:18:44.933 --> 00:18:47.200
of Meiji's long-term offensive in the Chinese mainland market.

00:18:47.200 --> 00:18:48.966
In 1997, its milk powder entered

00:18:49.066 --> 00:18:52.066
the Chinese market. In 2005, its Shanghai Songjiang chocolate factory was completed.

00:18:52.266 --> 00:18:54.666
By 2013, with the Suzhou factory going into operation,

00:18:54.666 --> 00:18:56.933
Meiji's fresh milk and yogurt were simultaneously launched

00:18:56.933 --> 00:18:57.933
in four locations in East China.

00:18:57.933 --> 00:18:59.866
In 2020, Meiji invested

00:18:59.866 --> 00:19:02.400
approximately 28 billion yen in Australia-Asia Dairy Farm

00:19:02.400 --> 00:19:04.300
, becoming one of the first foreign dairy companies to bring the Japanese-style low-temperature fresh milk

00:19:04.300 --> 00:19:05.900
and yogurt system

00:19:05.900 --> 00:19:08.566
to China's cold chain on a large scale.

00:19:08.900 --> 00:19:10.066
Looking back at its Japanese home base,

00:19:10.066 --> 00:19:11.800
Meiji began its transformation

00:19:11.800 --> 00:19:12.966
in the 21st century

00:19:12.966 --> 00:19:14.900
. In 2009, Meiji Holdings was established

00:19:14.900 --> 00:19:17.000
. In one year, the entire group split into two:

00:19:17.000 --> 00:19:19.466
Meiji Foods, focusing on food production,

00:19:19.500 --> 00:19:20.900
and Meiji Pharmaceutical

00:19:20.933 --> 00:19:22.666
, deeply involved in

00:19:22.866 --> 00:19:23.966
the pharmaceutical field

00:19:23.966 --> 00:19:25.066
. Since pharmaceuticals are rather boring

00:19:25.133 --> 00:19:27.066
, I won't go into detail.

00:19:27.066 --> 00:19:29.400
Actually, Meiji had already started producing penicillin as early as 1946.

00:19:29.400 --> 00:19:31.466
Today, Meiji is

00:19:31.466 --> 00:19:32.933
one of Japan's largest food giants.

00:19:33.166 --> 00:19:34.866
In the fiercely competitive dairy market

00:19:34.866 --> 00:19:37.066
, they have long held a leading position

00:19:37.066 --> 00:19:38.566
thanks to their various functional yogurts.

00:19:38.566 --> 00:19:39.300
In recent years,

00:19:39.300 --> 00:19:41.200
Meiji has made a big bet,

00:19:41.300 --> 00:19:43.000
fully transforming into a health food company.

00:19:43.000 --> 00:19:43.800
They are very clever.

00:19:43.800 --> 00:19:45.866
In the past, chocolate and snacks naturally

00:19:45.866 --> 00:19:48.400
carried the guilt of being high in calories and causing weight gain—

00:19:48.500 --> 00:19:49.600
an insurmountable ceiling

00:19:49.600 --> 00:19:51.400
for all confectionery companies.

00:19:51.400 --> 00:19:53.566
However, Meiji, leveraging its research background,

00:19:53.566 --> 00:19:55.900
has transformed the burden of snacking

00:19:55.900 --> 00:19:58.700
into a healthy way of eating chocolate

00:19:58.766 --> 00:20:00.166
through bottles of functional

00:20:00.166 --> 00:20:02.066
yogurts that focus on regulating bodily functions and bars of high-purity bitter chocolate

00:20:02.066 --> 00:20:03.900
. From the birth of the first Meiji milk chocolate

00:20:03.900 --> 00:20:05.500
in 1926 to today

00:20:05.500 --> 00:20:06.500
, a full 100 years,

00:20:06.666 --> 00:20:08.800
from a poor boy from a fallen samurai family

00:20:08.800 --> 00:20:10.466
to the colonial sugar business

00:20:10.566 --> 00:20:12.800
, then to the ruins of war and commercial battles, and

00:20:12.966 --> 00:20:14.766
finally back to the convenience store shelf

00:20:14.766 --> 00:20:15.700
for healthy eating—

00:20:15.700 --> 00:20:17.700
this is the story of Meiji today.

00:20:17.700 --> 00:20:18.500
Thank you.

